WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.490
OWARIMONOGATARI
SODACHI LOST

00:00:01.740 --> 00:00:06.120
<i>Back then, not even the few friends I had
knew my parents' profession.</i>

00:00:06.450 --> 00:00:09.000
<i>How in the world did Oikura find out?</i>

00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:13.670
<i>Such a curveball was tossed at me
by Hanekawa early yesterday morning.</i>

00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:16.460
QUESTION

00:00:16.630 --> 00:00:20.220
<i>I couldn't answer.
I had no idea whatsoever.</i>

00:00:20.380 --> 00:00:25.720
If you can't figure it out no matter what you do,
how about you go ask your parents?

00:00:25.930 --> 00:00:28.520
<i>Sure enough, that shed some light
on the answer.</i>

00:00:28.770 --> 00:00:34.350
<i>Oikura and I had met back in grade school...
In other words, we're childhood friends.</i>

00:00:34.730 --> 00:00:38.270
<i>To be precise, it was somewhere
back around when I was in sixth grade...</i>

00:00:38.530 --> 00:00:41.900
<i>Back around when I was playing
with my little sister Tsukihi,</i>

00:00:41.900 --> 00:00:44.740
<i>or with Sengoku
and the others Tsukihi brought over.</i>

00:00:45.070 --> 00:00:47.780
<i>Back then, I was together
with Sodachi Oikura.</i>

00:00:48.660 --> 00:00:52.160
I don't have many memories
of my grade school days,

00:00:52.160 --> 00:00:55.920
so I clearly remember about
when I played with Tsukihi,

00:00:56.250 --> 00:00:59.300
though I called her Lala at the time.

00:00:59.500 --> 00:01:01.800
Of course, I remember about you too,
Big Brother Koyomi.

00:01:03.050 --> 00:01:03.800
<i>There you have it.</i>

00:01:04.590 --> 00:01:09.220
<i>One day... Wait, though I am speaking
as if I remember all of this now,</i>

00:01:09.220 --> 00:01:12.180
<i>I haven't remembered any of this
as being reality just yet.</i>

00:01:12.180 --> 00:01:13.810
<i>I have no memory of it at all.</i>

00:01:14.100 --> 00:01:17.560
<i>This is what my parents told me
when I asked them, that's all.</i>

00:01:18.020 --> 00:01:19.070
<i>In any case, one day...</i>

00:01:19.650 --> 00:01:23.320
<i>My parents came home
and brought a girl with them.</i>

00:01:23.530 --> 00:01:27.320
<i>That girl was, of course,
who is now known to be Sodachi Oikura.</i>

00:01:28.120 --> 00:01:32.410
<i>My parents didn't give much of an explanation,
but apparently told me and my two younger sisters</i>

00:01:32.410 --> 00:01:35.830
<i>that she'd be staying with us for a while,
so we should be friends.</i>

00:01:36.460 --> 00:01:40.590
<i>My parents had taken Oikura as a child
to protect her from her "family,"</i>

00:01:40.590 --> 00:01:42.760
<i>and brought her to their own home.</i>

00:01:43.300 --> 00:01:48.220
<i>From her "family," where it was seen
that violence was already rampant at that time.</i>

00:01:48.600 --> 00:01:51.350
I thought that she was
something of a mysterious person.

00:01:51.600 --> 00:01:53.730
She never tried to play with us,

00:01:53.730 --> 00:01:57.600
but didn't attempt to leave the room either,
and she never spoke.

00:01:58.020 --> 00:02:00.610
<i>However, she suddenly disappeared.</i>

00:02:01.230 --> 00:02:07.360
<i>Naturally, it was simply the fact that the child Oikura
had returned to her own house of her own accord.</i>

00:02:07.660 --> 00:02:08.870
<i>She did so voluntarily.</i>

00:02:09.570 --> 00:02:11.870
<i>It wasn't that her parents
came to take her back,</i>

00:02:11.870 --> 00:02:16.120
<i>or my parents were no longer able
to protect her due to certain circumstances...</i>

00:02:16.500 --> 00:02:18.750
<i>The child Oikura had decided on her own,</i>

00:02:18.750 --> 00:02:22.750
<i>and left my version of "our home,"
and returned to her version of "our home."</i>

00:03:55.220 --> 00:03:56.640
OWARIMONOGATARI

00:03:56.640 --> 00:03:58.520
OWARIMONOGATARI
SODACHI LOST, PART TWO

00:03:58.520 --> 00:03:59.600
OWARIMONOGATARI
SODACHI LOST

00:03:59.600 --> 00:04:01.190
How dare you come here.

00:04:01.190 --> 00:04:02.020
OIKURA'S CONDO, ENTRANCE

00:04:02.400 --> 00:04:06.190
I'll commend you on your nerve, Ararag—

00:04:06.610 --> 00:04:07.360
ARARA-G?

00:04:10.240 --> 00:04:12.610
Your name is so hard to pronounth...

00:04:13.870 --> 00:04:14.700
SAME, DINING ROOM

00:04:15.120 --> 00:04:19.540
Well... You look like
you're doing well, Oikura. I'm glad.

00:04:19.540 --> 00:04:22.250
Look like I'm doing well?
Does it look that way?

00:04:23.540 --> 00:04:27.090
Really. Just how much
of a hypocrite is she?

00:04:27.090 --> 00:04:30.380
I'd suspected she wasn't just
some quiet, frail little girl...

00:04:30.760 --> 00:04:33.390
Maybe I should sue her
for bodily injury.

00:04:33.590 --> 00:04:37.810
Like, go to the doctor before the swelling goes down
and get a certificate for my injuries.

00:04:37.810 --> 00:04:41.390
That way, maybe her recommendation
for college enrollment will be withdrawn?

00:04:48.440 --> 00:04:50.190
Wait... what?

00:04:50.360 --> 00:04:53.820
Wh-What is it?
Why are you poking my cheek?

00:04:54.070 --> 00:04:55.200
Like, poke-poke...

00:04:55.370 --> 00:04:59.290
Are we close enough that
you could act so mischievously with me?

00:04:59.290 --> 00:05:01.830
What crime do you want
to be prosecuted for?

00:05:02.210 --> 00:05:07.210
With that cheek, you probably wouldn't get
a certificate for injuries from any doctor, Oikura.

00:05:10.800 --> 00:05:11.670
What?

00:05:14.590 --> 00:05:19.310
The swelling completely healed in two nights.
What a healing power I have...

00:05:19.560 --> 00:05:22.310
It seems like you're doing well,
with no major problems.

00:05:22.600 --> 00:05:26.270
So, starting tomorrow,
you'll come to school again, right, Oikura?

00:05:26.520 --> 00:05:30.030
So this is your job
as class president, huh? Let's see...

00:05:30.280 --> 00:05:32.610
...Hanekawa, was it?

00:05:32.610 --> 00:05:35.110
Right. I'm Tsubasa Hanekawa.

00:05:36.070 --> 00:05:39.910
So you were asked by our teacher
to come pick me up or something?

00:05:41.160 --> 00:05:42.870
Hanekawa aside...

00:05:43.790 --> 00:05:45.870
Why would you come here?

00:05:46.120 --> 00:05:47.000
A...

00:05:47.000 --> 00:05:48.880
A-ra-ra-gi.

00:05:50.000 --> 00:05:52.590
I don't want to see your face,

00:05:52.590 --> 00:05:55.630
and I'm sure you don't want
to see my face either, you know?

00:05:55.880 --> 00:06:00.350
You know, I thought we really
didn't get along with each other.

00:06:00.350 --> 00:06:02.770
Was that just my misunderstanding?

00:06:03.060 --> 00:06:04.520
It's not a misunderstanding.

00:06:04.730 --> 00:06:06.770
But, it wasn't only that, either...

00:06:08.020 --> 00:06:11.520
Weren't you the one who taught me that
the day before yesterday?

00:06:14.150 --> 00:06:15.740
And even back in grade school.

00:06:31.290 --> 00:06:35.590
No, well, I thought it'd be dangerous
if you threw the tea, Oikura.

00:06:35.590 --> 00:06:38.010
So I prepared myself beforehand...

00:06:39.300 --> 00:06:43.100
Two days ago, I couldn't stop Senjyogahara,
so I thought things over.

00:06:44.470 --> 00:06:45.480
THINKING THINGS OVER
CAME TO BE OF TOO GOOD A USE.

00:06:45.480 --> 00:06:46.850
Oikura.

00:06:47.600 --> 00:06:48.980
Let's have a chat...

00:06:49.350 --> 00:06:50.480
...about the past.

00:06:51.020 --> 00:06:52.480
About the past for you and me.

00:06:52.480 --> 00:06:54.150
IN THE END, THE ONE FACING OFF
AGAINST OIKURA WASN'T HANEKAWA, BUT ME.

00:06:58.570 --> 00:07:00.620
I despise you.

00:07:00.620 --> 00:07:02.120
OWARIMONOGATARI
SODACHI LOST

00:07:02.370 --> 00:07:03.870
Now you remember...

00:07:03.870 --> 00:07:07.580
From the look of it, not only did you remember,
but, after five years,

00:07:07.580 --> 00:07:11.880
it finally got through to you
what I was trying to do back then.

00:07:12.250 --> 00:07:16.510
Which means...
you must totally be making fun of me.

00:07:16.800 --> 00:07:20.510
Of someone who was totally kissing up to you
in order to get some help...

00:07:22.050 --> 00:07:23.260
Of myself.

00:07:23.720 --> 00:07:24.850
Kissing up?

00:07:25.020 --> 00:07:26.600
I-I'm an idiot.

00:07:26.770 --> 00:07:28.730
I'm an idiot, I'm an idiot, I'm an idiot.

00:07:29.140 --> 00:07:30.850
I really am such an idiot!

00:07:31.100 --> 00:07:35.230
I-I'm so embarrassed that I tried to save myself
when it meant kissing up to a guy like this!

00:07:35.610 --> 00:07:39.490
I threw out my pride back then
to flatter someone like this!

00:07:39.860 --> 00:07:42.990
I licked and lapped his shoes,
at least emotionally!

00:07:45.290 --> 00:07:49.250
In the hope of making up for my mistakes,
I made an even worse one...

00:07:49.250 --> 00:07:50.920
Embarrassing, embarrassing!

00:07:50.920 --> 00:07:54.790
Embarrassing, embarrassing...
I want to die! I want to be gone!

00:07:58.760 --> 00:08:00.220
But, Araragi.

00:08:01.010 --> 00:08:05.180
Even if it wasn't me,
I'm sure the same thing would've happened.

00:08:05.350 --> 00:08:08.180
I don't think I was
especially unfortunate or anything.

00:08:08.180 --> 00:08:10.440
Something like this happens often.

00:08:12.900 --> 00:08:15.690
Hey, don't you think so, too?

00:08:15.900 --> 00:08:18.940
You can't possibly be feeling sympathetic
towards me or anything, right?

00:08:20.570 --> 00:08:22.990
Don't pity me...

00:08:22.990 --> 00:08:27.830
If you, someone who I despise,
pities me, I really feel like I want to die.

00:08:29.790 --> 00:08:33.580
I do feel like it can't be helped,
no matter what you tell me.

00:08:33.580 --> 00:08:37.840
Because I haven't returned one bit
of what you've given me.

00:08:38.170 --> 00:08:41.220
So if you're telling me not to pity me,
then I won't pity you.

00:08:41.420 --> 00:08:44.720
If you're saying not to atone for it,
of course I won't atone, either.

00:08:45.350 --> 00:08:48.430
What's up with that?
Are you trying to act tough?

00:08:48.430 --> 00:08:51.100
Do you think an attitude like that
is especially manly?

00:08:51.100 --> 00:08:54.150
Do you think doing something like that
makes you a superior human?

00:08:54.310 --> 00:08:58.780
Manly? That's just you tossing everything out.

00:08:58.780 --> 00:09:02.530
Yeah... but speaking of tossing out,
didn't you do the same thing?

00:09:09.950 --> 00:09:13.580
I couldn't help it. That's not my fault.

00:09:13.580 --> 00:09:14.960
Why I toss things out,

00:09:14.960 --> 00:09:18.130
why I run away when I'm sick of it,
is all my parents' fault.

00:09:18.130 --> 00:09:19.380
My parents are the ones at fault.

00:09:19.670 --> 00:09:22.130
It's my parents' responsibility
that I ended up like this.

00:09:23.930 --> 00:09:25.890
So what are those parents doing now?

00:09:26.050 --> 00:09:28.560
Whoa! Why is that on your mind?

00:09:28.560 --> 00:09:30.350
I mean, the family makeup
of someone like me.

00:09:30.640 --> 00:09:33.690
You didn't even consider it at all
back in middle school.

00:09:35.440 --> 00:09:39.400
After you failed to help me,
they happily got a divorce.

00:09:39.940 --> 00:09:43.860
My mother got custody of me,
and I left this town...

00:09:44.780 --> 00:09:48.660
I don't give a rat's ass about
what the male parent is doing nowadays.

00:09:48.870 --> 00:09:52.200
That's right. That male parent
is the one who did all that to that house.

00:09:52.410 --> 00:09:53.410
That scumbag.

00:09:54.080 --> 00:09:59.540
My mother only hit me when she needed to vent
the frustration of being beaten by the male parent.

00:10:00.130 --> 00:10:04.050
I've been cooped up in my place like this
for over two years now.

00:10:07.340 --> 00:10:10.060
But my mother also
cooped herself up as well.

00:10:10.310 --> 00:10:13.020
Right after we turned into
a fatherless family, too...

00:10:13.020 --> 00:10:15.810
It seems like the divorce gradually got to her.

00:10:15.810 --> 00:10:19.810
She cooped herself up in one room
of our new home, and she never left it.

00:10:20.070 --> 00:10:21.400
Never left?

00:10:21.690 --> 00:10:23.570
It really was horrible.

00:10:23.990 --> 00:10:27.700
She cooped herself up inside a locked room
and curled up in a corner.

00:10:27.910 --> 00:10:31.280
Eventually, she stopped eating altogether.

00:10:31.280 --> 00:10:36.290
Mother boarded up all the windows
and kept the curtains closed.

00:10:36.540 --> 00:10:38.420
The room was pitch black.

00:10:40.090 --> 00:10:43.130
And for the longest time,
she kept mumbling.

00:10:43.340 --> 00:10:47.380
She mumbled stuff like,
"Parents can't choose their children," and stuff.

00:10:47.550 --> 00:10:51.600
But at some point, she started to ignore me,
no matter what I said to her.

00:10:52.810 --> 00:10:56.940
Fortunately, Japan is a country
that's pretty substantial in providing welfare.

00:10:57.100 --> 00:11:00.560
Even without my mother earning a living,
as long as you have the proper paperwork,

00:11:00.560 --> 00:11:03.020
one parent and one child
could barely scrape by.

00:11:03.020 --> 00:11:08.740
So "it'd be better if my mother was gone"
was something I've never once thought.

00:11:08.740 --> 00:11:11.030
This is one thing that's true.

00:11:13.490 --> 00:11:16.580
Because I was praying every night...

00:11:16.580 --> 00:11:22.000
So that "it'd be better if my mother was gone"
would be something I wouldn't wish for.

00:11:22.710 --> 00:11:27.720
So that "it'd be better if my mother was gone"
would be something I wouldn't wish for.

00:11:28.470 --> 00:11:33.260
So that "it'd be better if my mother was gone"
would be something I wouldn't wish for.

00:11:33.430 --> 00:11:38.850
So that "it'd be better if my mother was gone"
would be something I wouldn't wish for.

00:11:40.150 --> 00:11:44.980
But, my mother was gone,
against my wishes.

00:11:44.980 --> 00:11:47.110
AGAINST MY WISHES

00:11:49.070 --> 00:11:51.530
One day, without telling me anything,

00:11:51.530 --> 00:11:55.580
without confessing anything to me,
my mother was gone.

00:11:56.410 --> 00:11:59.790
When I came home from school,
my mother was gone.

00:11:59.790 --> 00:12:02.130
My mother was gone then.

00:12:02.420 --> 00:12:05.340
Suddenly, without any warning,
she went off somewhere...

00:12:05.340 --> 00:12:08.010
See, isn't that a lot like me?

00:12:08.260 --> 00:12:11.800
They say that girls often tend to be
more like their male parents,

00:12:11.800 --> 00:12:14.220
but I'm sure I'm a lot like my mother.

00:12:14.220 --> 00:12:15.510
OIKURA, MOST LIKELY

00:12:16.890 --> 00:12:18.390
SMILED LIKE HER MOTHER.

00:12:18.390 --> 00:12:19.890
OWARIMONOGATARI
SODACHI LOST

00:12:20.560 --> 00:12:23.360
I made dinner
and took it up to her room.

00:12:23.730 --> 00:12:27.150
I unlocked the door and went inside,
and it was completely empty.

00:12:27.400 --> 00:12:29.650
There wasn't even a letter left behind.

00:12:29.940 --> 00:12:31.280
My parents...

00:12:31.280 --> 00:12:32.030
OIKURA SAYS THAT.

00:12:32.320 --> 00:12:33.370
Both of them...

00:12:33.370 --> 00:12:34.240
KILLING EMOTIONS

00:12:34.490 --> 00:12:36.580
I have no idea
of their whereabouts anymore.

00:12:36.580 --> 00:12:37.950
SLAUGHTERING HER OWN HEART

00:12:38.160 --> 00:12:42.500
In any case, with that,
I was freed from taking care of my mother.

00:12:42.500 --> 00:12:44.580
I was able to catch up
on my schoolwork as well.

00:12:44.830 --> 00:12:48.170
Among my relatives, I found someone
that could be my legal guardian in name only.

00:12:48.170 --> 00:12:51.970
And then, by receiving federal aid,
I was able to come back to this town.

00:12:52.340 --> 00:12:56.470
I didn't want to see you,
so I really didn't want to come back here...

00:12:56.890 --> 00:12:58.890
But this was the only place
that had an opening.

00:12:59.350 --> 00:13:01.890
Why did you decide to live on your own?

00:13:02.190 --> 00:13:06.400
You could've continued to live in the house
where you had lived with your mother.

00:13:06.820 --> 00:13:09.030
Why did you decide to take the time
to move at that point?

00:13:09.320 --> 00:13:11.070
Because it was a place
overfilled with garbage.

00:13:11.070 --> 00:13:14.860
I felt it better to toss out the entire house,
rather than attempt to clean up at that point.

00:13:15.160 --> 00:13:19.040
Thinking over my past,
I keep the amount of furniture here sparse.

00:13:19.240 --> 00:13:21.200
It looks really neat here, doesn't it?

00:13:22.120 --> 00:13:26.210
You get it now...
that I'm not that unfortunate?

00:13:26.210 --> 00:13:29.420
Something at this level
could happen to anyone, can't it?

00:13:29.710 --> 00:13:32.300
Some more, some less,
but everyone experiences it.

00:13:32.550 --> 00:13:36.800
It's something commonplace...
or rather, it's not even a story about hardships.

00:13:37.180 --> 00:13:40.470
Well, it might be a bit rougher
than for most people, sure.

00:13:40.470 --> 00:13:43.440
But if you say that,
you really can't get by in this world.

00:13:43.730 --> 00:13:48.190
If put on the spot, I guess your parent
cooping themselves up is something unusual.

00:13:48.190 --> 00:13:53.450
But I should be happy that I got to experience
something that doesn't happen often, a rarity.

00:13:53.650 --> 00:13:57.490
It's not like I'm the only unfortunate one,
so I have to do my best.

00:13:57.490 --> 00:14:01.830
I'm one of the more fortunate ones,
because I'm still alive like this.

00:14:03.460 --> 00:14:06.460
So, I'm saying you don't have to pity me...

00:14:06.460 --> 00:14:09.840
You don't have to apologize
or atone for anything, Araragi.

00:14:10.050 --> 00:14:13.130
You don't have to
make up for your sins at all.

00:14:13.590 --> 00:14:15.970
Somehow, talking about this
has cleared my mind, too...

00:14:17.590 --> 00:14:20.600
In the end, they're all stories of the past.

00:14:20.600 --> 00:14:24.890
The stories of the past that you seek
are only stories of the distant past.

00:14:24.890 --> 00:14:26.850
They're all stories that have concluded.

00:14:26.850 --> 00:14:28.310
END

00:14:28.310 --> 00:14:31.270
I was irritated,
so I lashed out at you,

00:14:31.270 --> 00:14:34.820
but at this point, I don't feel like
I want you to do anything for me.

00:14:35.200 --> 00:14:36.200
If anything...

00:14:37.820 --> 00:14:39.570
...can you guys go home now?

00:14:41.870 --> 00:14:42.580
IF SHE TELLS US TO GO HOME,

00:14:42.870 --> 00:14:43.540
WE HAVE NO CHOICE BUT TO GO HOME.

00:14:43.750 --> 00:14:45.370
- Oi—
- Oikura.

00:14:45.370 --> 00:14:47.420
Did you say "unlock the door"?

00:14:47.670 --> 00:14:48.540
What?

00:14:51.800 --> 00:14:53.300
Yes. That's right.

00:14:53.710 --> 00:14:58.050
When you unlocked the door and went in,
your mother was gone...

00:14:58.050 --> 00:15:01.390
But the windows were all boarded up, right?

00:15:01.390 --> 00:15:04.020
And if the door was locked on top of that,

00:15:04.270 --> 00:15:06.810
where did your mother
leave the room from?

00:15:09.020 --> 00:15:10.110
OWARIMONOGATARI
SODACHI LOST

00:15:10.110 --> 00:15:11.520
WHERE DID YOUR MOTHER LEAVE THE ROOM FROM?

00:15:12.400 --> 00:15:13.440
A LOCKED ROOM

00:15:13.730 --> 00:15:17.200
From where? From the door, of course.

00:15:17.200 --> 00:15:21.830
The door unlocks if you turn the inside handle,
so you can leave that way.

00:15:22.030 --> 00:15:24.200
Then, was it a door
that locks itself automatically?

00:15:24.410 --> 00:15:26.160
It was a normal keyed door.

00:15:27.210 --> 00:15:32.960
But the key was placed randomly
somewhere around the house,

00:15:32.960 --> 00:15:35.630
so I'm sure my mother
locked the door before leaving.

00:15:37.260 --> 00:15:40.680
Well, yeah. You're right.

00:15:41.510 --> 00:15:45.770
Then, Oikura, setting aside the room's lock,
what about the lock on the front door?

00:15:46.640 --> 00:15:49.020
Why do you want to know
something so trivial as that....

00:15:49.520 --> 00:15:51.020
I don't really remember.

00:15:51.190 --> 00:15:54.690
If she doesn't remember,
that means it didn't make an impression on her.

00:15:54.690 --> 00:15:57.280
That probably means that the door
was properly locked, right?

00:15:57.610 --> 00:16:00.660
If it was unlocked, she would've felt
something was strange at that point.

00:16:02.030 --> 00:16:03.660
I just don't get it...

00:16:03.870 --> 00:16:08.160
Why does my mother's disappearance
bother you so much? Why?

00:16:09.040 --> 00:16:10.620
Hey, Araragi...

00:16:11.120 --> 00:16:15.130
Do you know how I felt when I was taken
into protective custody at your place?

00:16:16.210 --> 00:16:19.470
I wondered why
you guys were showing off.

00:16:19.470 --> 00:16:24.260
I had thought that my house,
and my family, was the norm.

00:16:24.260 --> 00:16:29.770
No broken windows, no cracked walls,
no cracked floors - a neat little house like that...

00:16:29.770 --> 00:16:33.400
I couldn't believe that
such a calm family could exist.

00:16:33.650 --> 00:16:36.150
That's why I kept glaring at
all of you the whole time.

00:16:36.520 --> 00:16:38.650
I silently kept glaring.

00:16:38.650 --> 00:16:39.650
Do you remember that?

00:16:40.860 --> 00:16:41.780
Yeah...

00:16:41.990 --> 00:16:42.950
A LIE.

00:16:42.950 --> 00:16:43.910
I HAVE NO MEMORY OF BACK THEN.

00:16:44.240 --> 00:16:47.830
It was so bright... that's why I ran away.

00:16:47.830 --> 00:16:51.330
I was blinded by the brightness,
and felt like my eyes would be crushed.

00:16:51.330 --> 00:16:53.000
My body was going to be crushed
by the warmth and comfort.

00:16:53.000 --> 00:16:53.710
I WISH I NEVER KNEW.

00:16:55.500 --> 00:16:56.170
I WISH...

00:16:56.170 --> 00:16:58.800
But it was no good. It was too late.

00:16:58.800 --> 00:16:59.630
I NEVER MET YOU.

00:16:59.630 --> 00:17:02.050
After seeing something like that just once...

00:17:02.050 --> 00:17:05.390
I realized just how miserable my house was.

00:17:05.390 --> 00:17:06.300
IT SHOULD HAVE BEEN A NORMAL HOUSE.

00:17:06.300 --> 00:17:07.390
SHE FELT THAT IT WAS BRIGHT.

00:17:08.930 --> 00:17:12.980
By the time I found out,
there was nothing I could do.

00:17:12.980 --> 00:17:16.980
I tried strange ways to do something about it,
and they started to say I was acting rebellious.

00:17:16.980 --> 00:17:19.440
That caused me
to be beaten even more often.

00:17:19.440 --> 00:17:21.150
Where it wouldn't be seen on me...

00:17:22.900 --> 00:17:24.530
...the parts of me that weren't visible...

00:17:26.570 --> 00:17:28.280
...were all pummeled.

00:17:30.040 --> 00:17:32.960
But upon escaping that,
I couldn't fully escape.

00:17:33.960 --> 00:17:35.710
I could no longer escape.

00:17:37.380 --> 00:17:42.590
That's why, when I was reunited with you
back in middle school, I felt like it was destiny.

00:17:47.470 --> 00:17:49.600
Didn't I do my best to kiss up to you?

00:17:51.220 --> 00:17:56.100
Well, in reaction to that,
when we had our second reunion in high school,

00:17:56.100 --> 00:17:58.480
I was a bit too harsh with you.

00:17:58.940 --> 00:18:03.490
In any case, you had forgotten about me,
so none of that really mattered.

00:18:05.030 --> 00:18:07.870
Really... things just don't go well.

00:18:07.870 --> 00:18:11.790
With Tetsujo gone, I finally thought
that I could start over this time.

00:18:12.000 --> 00:18:14.870
Araragi in my class yet again?
That's impossible.

00:18:14.870 --> 00:18:19.750
I really do feel something like destiny here.
A destiny much like a curse.

00:18:20.170 --> 00:18:25.930
You show up at every significant event in my life
and spread forth disaster.

00:18:26.840 --> 00:18:28.850
- It's my fault?
- That's right.

00:18:28.850 --> 00:18:31.970
Because of you,
my life is in shambles...

00:18:31.970 --> 00:18:37.400
No. I know it's not your fault.
I know that I'm the one at fault...

00:18:37.730 --> 00:18:40.400
What my mother said was correct.

00:18:40.400 --> 00:18:44.900
If the baby born wasn't me,
it would've been a decent one.

00:18:45.320 --> 00:18:47.610
It's my fault. I despise myself.

00:18:47.610 --> 00:18:49.620
I... I despise myself.

00:18:49.950 --> 00:18:54.500
But you know, if I don't blame it on you,
I can't keep going, Araragi.

00:18:54.500 --> 00:18:57.500
I'm sorry, but please be my villain.

00:18:57.500 --> 00:18:58.880
I can't take it anymore.

00:18:58.880 --> 00:19:03.250
I can't recover if my parents
are the only villains I blame.

00:19:03.590 --> 00:19:04.340
Oikura...

00:19:04.340 --> 00:19:06.840
I wonder why things
never go well for me.

00:19:06.840 --> 00:19:11.050
I'm doing things properly, I'm doing my best,
I'm making a good effort...

00:19:11.430 --> 00:19:15.640
Of course, personality or sanity included,
there are all sorts of strange things.

00:19:15.640 --> 00:19:19.900
But I haven't done anything that calls for
all the punishment I've received so far.

00:19:21.270 --> 00:19:25.990
Tell me, Araragi.
You're happy right now, right?

00:19:25.990 --> 00:19:31.660
If I'm contributing even just a little bit,
if you think that, tell me.

00:19:31.910 --> 00:19:35.160
Why can't I be happy?

00:19:36.200 --> 00:19:41.170
You're not happy because
you're not trying to be happy.

00:19:41.540 --> 00:19:46.420
Nobody can make someone who isn't trying
to be happy into someone that's happy.

00:19:47.380 --> 00:19:49.930
You sound like you know
what you're talking about.

00:19:50.180 --> 00:19:53.810
I don't know everything.
I only know what I know.

00:19:56.310 --> 00:19:59.310
Really, that's how it is. You're correct.

00:19:59.310 --> 00:20:00.190
ANSWER

00:20:00.440 --> 00:20:06.230
I mean, considering how frail I am,
if I was happy, I'd get crushed. Like, crunch.

00:20:06.230 --> 00:20:11.320
My eyes, my body, they'd be crushed.
I couldn't bear the weight of happiness.

00:20:11.320 --> 00:20:13.070
Instead of being happy after all this,

00:20:13.070 --> 00:20:17.410
I rather be steeped ankle-deep in
lukewarm unhappiness and bear all of it.

00:20:17.410 --> 00:20:20.250
I want to keep my shoes soaking wet
for as long as I live.

00:20:20.540 --> 00:20:22.580
In reality, that's what I've been doing...

00:20:22.880 --> 00:20:23.670
Yup.

00:20:24.540 --> 00:20:27.090
I can't be happy after all this.

00:20:27.260 --> 00:20:28.590
It's already too late.

00:20:28.590 --> 00:20:29.420
TOO LATE.

00:20:29.420 --> 00:20:30.760
THEN WHEN WOULD IT HAVE BEEN
CONSIDERED MAKING IT IN TIME?

00:20:30.760 --> 00:20:31.930
OR, WAS IT THAT WAY BEFORE THAT,
IT WAS ALREADY TOO LATE—

00:20:31.930 --> 00:20:32.970
MY CHILDHOOD FRIEND.

00:20:32.970 --> 00:20:34.220
EVERYTHING WAS A THING OF THE PAST,
HARDLY WORTH MENTIONING,

00:20:34.220 --> 00:20:35.430
WAS IT SOMETHING THAT COULDN'T BE UNDONE,
UNABLE TO RETURN, AND TOO LATE FOR IT—

00:20:35.430 --> 00:20:35.930
NO.

00:20:35.930 --> 00:20:36.510
INCORRECT.

00:20:36.510 --> 00:20:37.350
THAT'S NOT HOW IT IS.

00:20:37.350 --> 00:20:38.350
No way.

00:20:39.680 --> 00:20:43.650
There's no happiness that's so heavy
you'd be crushed by it.

00:20:43.650 --> 00:20:46.650
Happiness isn't bright or heavy.

00:20:46.650 --> 00:20:48.490
Don't overestimate what happiness is.

00:20:49.740 --> 00:20:53.160
All kinds of happiness
are perfect for you.

00:20:53.820 --> 00:20:56.660
So don't despise happiness like that.

00:20:56.660 --> 00:20:59.500
Don't despise the world,
don't despise anything and everything....

00:20:59.700 --> 00:21:01.290
Don't despise yourself.

00:21:01.750 --> 00:21:07.630
All the types of "despise" within your body...
I'll accept all of them for you. I'll accept them all.

00:21:07.960 --> 00:21:10.470
So I want you to love yourself more.

00:21:10.470 --> 00:21:10.970
YOU CAN DESPISE ME AS MUCH AS YOU WANT.

00:21:10.970 --> 00:21:11.720
YOU CAN DESPISE ME AS MUCH AS YOU WANT.
AT LEAST AS MUCH AS I

00:21:11.720 --> 00:21:13.010
YOU CAN DESPISE ME AS MUCH AS YOU WANT.
AT LEAST AS MUCH AS I
USED TO LOVE YOU BEFORE.

00:21:13.180 --> 00:21:17.600
It's true that I'm currently very happy...
that's why I'll make the effort to say this!

00:21:17.810 --> 00:21:21.520
It's a given that
everyone has something like this!

00:21:28.150 --> 00:21:29.400
Well said.

00:21:33.660 --> 00:21:34.740
Town hall...

00:21:35.320 --> 00:21:37.780
Someone from town hall is coming soon.

00:21:38.240 --> 00:21:42.160
I'm sorry to interrupt as you become passionate,
but I really want you guys to go home.

00:21:42.620 --> 00:21:46.170
They're going to come check
if I'm living a proper life.

00:21:46.540 --> 00:21:50.800
Right now, they're barely overlooking the fact
that I'm refusing to go to school.

00:21:51.090 --> 00:21:55.300
If they saw me arguing with my classmates,
I'd be in trouble.

00:21:55.510 --> 00:21:57.930
I see. Then we'll go home for today.

00:21:58.220 --> 00:22:00.720
But we'll come again tomorrow.
The day after, too.

00:22:00.720 --> 00:22:03.180
Not to mention the weekend,
even if it troubles you.

00:22:03.390 --> 00:22:09.190
Troubling those we care about
is how we do things.

00:22:13.320 --> 00:22:17.070
Oh, I forgot to tell you.
I should've said this at the beginning.

00:22:17.530 --> 00:22:20.910
I've grown to be pretty fond of you.

00:22:24.330 --> 00:22:29.130
Then, you guys...
please look for my mother who disappeared.

00:22:29.130 --> 00:22:32.090
If you can find her,
I wouldn't mind going to school again.

00:22:34.300 --> 00:24:20.234
And I wouldn't mind
apologizing to Senjyogahara.
